[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/comments/150809346","html_url":"https://github.com/xunit/xunit/issues/634#issuecomment-150809346","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/634","id":150809346,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE1MDgwOTM0Ng==","user":{"login":"jongleur1983","id":2063360,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjMzNjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2063360?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983","html_url":"https://github.com/jongleur1983","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-10-24T12:51:27Z","updated_at":"2015-10-24T12:51:27Z","body":"as far as I can see the problem is that `typeof(List<>).GetTypeInfo().GenericTypeParameters.First()`does return something like a Type placeholder, where TypeName is T, but FullName is null, as long as T is not set to a specific type.\n\nUsing `typeof(List<int>.GetTypeInfo().GenericTypeParameters.First()` works as expected of course.\n\nI traced it down to an exception silently handled in TheoryDiscoverer.Discover, digging further now.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/comments/150809346/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jongleur1983","id":2063360,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjMzNjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2063360?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983","html_url":"https://github.com/jongleur1983","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/comments/150832956","html_url":"https://github.com/xunit/xunit/issues/634#issuecomment-150832956","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/634","id":150832956,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE1MDgzMjk1Ng==","user":{"login":"jongleur1983","id":2063360,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjMzNjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2063360?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983","html_url":"https://github.com/jongleur1983","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-10-24T16:51:15Z","updated_at":"2015-10-24T16:51:15Z","body":"MSDN agrees with the behaviour of https://github.com/xunit/xunit/blob/6c62c646ef19ae1fb938447805afd132fa90d966/src/xunit.assert/Asserts/Sdk/ArgumentFormatter.cs#L174 here: https://msdn.microsoft.com/de-de/library/system.type.fullname%28v=vs.110%29.aspx , describing the value of `TypeInfo.FullName` as\n\n> The fully qualified name of the Type, [...]; or null if the current instance represents [...] a generic type that is not a generic type definition but contains unresolved type parameters.\n> This seems to be the case here, as `List<>` basically is `List<T>` with unresolved `T`.\n\nTherefore the bug is in fact in the ArgumentFormatter that currently assumes the FullName to be set on any type it get's.\n\nSo how to deal with it?\nI think `ArgumentFormatter.FormatTypeName(Type type)` should at least deal with this special case.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/comments/150832956/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jongleur1983","id":2063360,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjMzNjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2063360?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983","html_url":"https://github.com/jongleur1983","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/comments/150849761","html_url":"https://github.com/xunit/xunit/issues/634#issuecomment-150849761","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/634","id":150849761,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE1MDg0OTc2MQ==","user":{"login":"jongleur1983","id":2063360,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjMzNjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2063360?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983","html_url":"https://github.com/jongleur1983","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-10-24T20:50:39Z","updated_at":"2015-10-24T20:50:39Z","body":"locally I implemented tests covering that issue by directly invoking the ArgumentFormatter for unbound generic type arguments;\nIt would be easy to return the generic argument name in that case from `FormatTypeName()`; but as a result it would then return `typeof(T)` for a generic type argument that is named T, which seems not very useful at all.\nSo: what should be returned instead? anything like `typeof(?)` where `?` is replaced inside the brackets is easy to implement; but is it useful?\n\nI'll open a pull request that does return typeof(T) for a generic argument named T for now.\n\nany alternative solutions are welcome, and I'm fine with implementing them instead.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/comments/150849761/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jongleur1983","id":2063360,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjMzNjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2063360?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983","html_url":"https://github.com/jongleur1983","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jongleur1983/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"actor":{"login":"jongleur1983","id":2063360,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjMzNjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2063360?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https: